---
description: PyTorch training / eval loop guardrails.
globs: **/ml/**/*.py,**/training/**/*.py,**/notebooks/**/*.py,**/*.ipynb
alwaysApply: false
---

Every custom training loop MUST:

1. Wrap eval/validation in `with torch.no_grad():` AND call `model.eval()`; restore `model.train()` after.
2. Zero grads with `optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)`.
3. Step the LR scheduler at ONE documented cadence (per-step OR per-epoch, never both).
4. Move tensors with `.to(device, non_blocking=True)`; DataLoader uses `pin_memory=True` on CUDA.
5. Detach tensors before logging (`.detach().cpu().item()`).

GOOD: `model.eval(); with torch.no_grad(): for x,y in val_loader: ...; model.train()`.
